-- title:
--   Infinitesimal twist of an affine chart is an automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ and $B_1$ be commutative rings with $B_1$ a $B$-algebra whose structure map $B \to B_1$ is surjective and whose kernel $I$ satisfies $I \cdot I = (0)$. Let $f \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} B$ and $f_1 \colon X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} B_1$ be morphisms of schemes and $g \colon X_1 \to X$ a morphism such that the square formed by $g$, $f_1$, $f$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $B \to B_1$ is a pullback square (`IsPullback`). Let $U$ be an open of $X$ which is an affine open, write $C = \Gamma(X, U)$, viewed as a $B$-algebra through the map $B \to \Gamma(X,U)$ obtained from $f$ by `algebraOfHom` (the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism followed by $f$'s `appLE` from $\top$ to $U$). Let $v \colon \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$ satisfy: $v$ followed by $f$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $B \to C$; and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $C \to C/IC$, where $IC$ is the ideal generated by the image of $I$, followed by either $v$ or by `hU.fromSpec` (the canonical map $\operatorname{Spec} C \to X$) gives the same morphism. Then there is an isomorphism $\alpha$ of the open subscheme $U$ with itself such that the inverse of `hU.isoSpec` followed by $\alpha$ and the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X$ equals $v$; $\alpha$ followed by the inclusion and $f$ equals the inclusion followed by $f$; and the restriction $g \mid_U \colon g^{-1}(U) \to U$ followed by $\alpha$ equals $g \mid_U$.
--
--   This is a rigidity statement for first-order thickenings: a $B$-morphism $\operatorname{Spec} \Gamma(X,U) \to X$ agreeing with the inclusion of the affine chart $U$ modulo a square-zero ideal is the inclusion twisted by an automorphism of $U$ over $B$ which is the identity on the reduction along $g$. It is used in the construction of regluing data and of tangent coordinates on overlaps for bare deformations in the study of good reduction of Jacobians.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_iso_isoSpec_inv_comp_eq_of_specMap_comp_eq.lean

import Mathlib
